            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0283" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5561/22a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-06T13:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. The following announcement will be made to the press at 12:30 p.m. today:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The following changes in our representation in Moscow have been
                            ordered:</p>
                        <p>The Naval Attaché will be withdrawn.</p>
                        <p>The Air Attaché will be withdrawn.</p>
                        <p>The Consulate General will be abolished.</p>
                        <p>Reductions will be made in the personnel of the Embassy.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Inform Nimmer and White.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
